menuconfig ZMK_LED_CONFIG
    bool "Runtime-configurable extender LED (torabo-tsuki)"
    help
      Per-side rule table for the 3-colour extender LED — "when X happens, show
      colour C with pattern P" — editable live over BLE from Torabo-Studio.

      Supersedes TORABO_STATUS_LED_EXT, whose two behaviours (BLE profile flash,
      steady red while the other half is gone) are hardcoded and central-only.
      Do not enable both: they would fight over the same GPIOs.

      The central holds the whole table, decides what BOTH LEDs show, drives its
      own and pushes the peripheral's over the split — so the peripheral needs no
      config and nothing to sync. The one thing it decides for itself is what to
      show when the link is down, since the central cannot reach it then.

      Default n; enable per build target (see the torabo-led-live snippet).

if ZMK_LED_CONFIG

config ZMK_LED_CONFIG_BLE
    bool "Expose the LED rules over a BLE GATT service"
    depends on BT
    default y
    help
      Encrypted GATT service e1f4ae00 to read/write the rule table live. 72 B, so
      it fits in a single ATT write and needs no Write Long.

config ZMK_LED_CONFIG_LEFT_PRESENT
    bool "An LED exists on the left half"
    default n
    help
      Advertised to the app in the wire's capability byte, so it shows only the
      sides this keyboard actually has instead of assuming a layout. The LED's
      anode rides the extender pad's power rail, so this should only be y when the
      left half has an extender pad. The firmware builder sets it.

config ZMK_LED_CONFIG_RIGHT_PRESENT
    bool "An LED exists on the right half"
    default n
    help
      See LEFT_PRESENT.

config ZMK_LED_CONFIG_CENTRAL_IS_LEFT
    bool "The central half is the left one"
    default n
    help
      Tells the rule engine which array slot is local and which is reached over
      the split, and is advertised to the app. The firmware builder sets it.

module = ZMK_LED_CONFIG
module-str = ZMK LED Config
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ZMK_LED_CONFIG
